  "raw_response": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return grid\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h else 0\n    \n    points = []\n    color = 0\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                points.append((r, c))\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                \n    if not points:\n        return grid\n        \n    points.sort()\n    rows = [p[0] for p in points]\n    cols = [p[1] for p in points]\n    \n    d = 0\n    for i in range(1, len(points)):\n        d = math.gcd(d, abs(rows[i] - rows[i-1]))\n        d = math.gcd(d, abs(cols[i] - cols[i-1]))\n    if d == 0:\n        d = 1\n        \n    cr, cc = points[len(points) // 2]\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    out[cr][cc] = color\n    \n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        r1 = cr - k * d\n        r2 = cr + k * d\n        c1 = cc - k * d\n        c2 = cc + k * d\n        \n        if r2 < 0 or r1 >= h or c2 < 0 or c1 >= w:\n            break\n            \n        if r1 < 0 and r2 >= h and c1 < 0 and c2 >= w:\n            break\n            \n        rr1 = max(r1, 0)\n        rr2 = min(r2, h - 1)\n        cc1 = max(c1, 0)\n        cc2 = min(c2, w - 1)\n        \n        if r1 >= 0:\n            for c in range(cc1, cc2 + 1):\n                out[r1][c] = color\n        if r2 < h:\n            for c in range(cc1, cc2 + 1):\n                out[r2][c] = color\n        if c1 >= 0:\n            for r in range(rr1, rr2 + 1):\n                out[r][c1] = color\n        if c2 < w:\n            for r in range(rr1, rr2 + 1):\n                out[r][c2] = color\n                \n        k += 1\n        \n    return out\n```",
  "script": "import math\n\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return grid\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h else 0\n    \n    points = []\n    color = 0\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                points.append((r, c))\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                \n    if not points:\n        return grid\n        \n    points.sort()\n    rows = [p[0] for p in points]\n    cols = [p[1] for p in points]\n    \n    d = 0\n    for i in range(1, len(points)):\n        d = math.gcd(d, abs(rows[i] - rows[i-1]))\n        d = math.gcd(d, abs(cols[i] - cols[i-1]))\n    if d == 0:\n        d = 1\n        \n    cr, cc = points[len(points) // 2]\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    out[cr][cc] = color\n    \n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        r1 = cr - k * d\n        r2 = cr + k * d\n        c1 = cc - k * d\n        c2 = cc + k * d\n        \n        if r2 < 0 or r1 >= h or c2 < 0 or c1 >= w:\n            break\n            \n        if r1 < 0 and r2 >= h and c1 < 0 and c2 >= w:\n            break\n            \n        rr1 = max(r1, 0)\n        rr2 = min(r2, h - 1)\n        cc1 = max(c1, 0)\n        cc2 = min(c2, w - 1)\n        \n        if r1 >= 0:\n            for c in range(cc1, cc2 + 1):\n                out[r1][c] = color\n        if r2 < h:\n            for c in range(cc1, cc2 + 1):\n                out[r2][c] = color\n        if c1 >= 0:\n            for r in range(rr1, rr2 + 1):\n                out[r][c1] = color\n        if c2 < w:\n            for r in range(rr1, rr2 + 1):\n                out[r][c2] = color\n                \n        k += 1\n        \n    return out",
